// automations.memql -- the deploy pack (examples/deploypack), Epic 2.
//
// THE CORE PORT (E2.3 / #2096): the deploy lifecycle that
// component/deploycontrol/deploy.go + driver.go drive imperatively (pending ->
// in_progress -> apply the azure effect -> succeeded | failed) is modeled here
// as event-driven DSL automations, keyed off the deployment status transition
// the CDC path emits (graph.node.updated.v1:cluster:deployment). Each transition
// fires the matching IntegrationProvider effect from E2.2 (#2095).
//
// MODEL A RECORD-BACK (E2.4 / #2097): after the pack commits the overlay and
// ArgoCD reconciles, the reconciled state (synced / healthy + per-node spec) is
// observed and recorded back into the deployment concept -- the GitOps-canonical
// loop. The committed overlay stays the source of truth; the data layer mirrors
// the observed state.
//
// SAFETY (live deploy path): drives the SAME azure effect the Go orchestrator
// drives -- deployRunPromote -> Executor.RunPromote -> scripts/release/promote.sh
// via the Argo Rollout. No behavioral change vs deploy.go for the azure
// provider. ADDITIVE: the Go orchestrator is NOT removed here (that is E2.5);
// these automations only load when the deploy pack is mounted (build tag
// `deploypack`), so they never fire in a default binary.

use deploypack.logic.{ driveDeploymentInProgress, recordReconciledState }

@enabled
@trigger(event="graph.node.updated.v1:cluster:deployment")
@description("Event-driven port of deploy.go's apply+transition: when a v1:cluster:deployment enters in_progress for the azure provider, fire the deployRunPromote effect (the live azure deploy via promote.sh + Argo Rollout) and transition the record to succeeded on a clean promote or failed on a reported failure. Epic 2 / #2096.")
automation driveDeploymentInProgress {
  step run {
    logic driveDeploymentInProgress { event: event }
  }
}

// ---- automations/deploypack/recordReconciledState ----

@enabled
@trigger(event="graph.node.updated.v1:cluster:deployment")
@description("Model A record-back loop (#2097): when a v1:cluster:deployment reaches succeeded (the promote completed), observe the ArgoCD-reconciled state and append it back into the deployment concept -- the per-node readiness via createDeploymentNodeSpec and, only when ArgoCD reports NOT synced/healthy, a corrective transition. The committed overlay stays the source of truth; the data layer mirrors the observed state. Multi-node safe: the append is idempotent and the guard keeps it from re-triggering itself. Epic 2 / #2097.")
automation recordReconciledState {
  step run {
    logic recordReconciledState { event: event }
  }
}
